  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Life Saving Response through the Prepositioning and Provision of Emergency Shelter and NFIs Support to Flood Affected Areas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Over a decade, South Sudan continues to experience national and sub-national-level conflicts that have destabilized the country, forcing over 8.9 million people to flee their homes in search of protection and physical security. IOM is contributing to preventing, reducing and responding to the needs of flood-affected and flood prone communities through the provision of in-kind Shelter and non-food item (S-NFI) assistance. Through this project, IOM&#x2019;s Core Pipeline is contributing to lifesaving efforts of the expected floods in South Sudan by prepositioning of essential S-NFIs supplies at key logistic warehouse hubs in Juba, Bentiu, Bor, Malakal, Rumbek and Wau, to support frontline emergency Shelter and NFIs for populations displaced by floods.</narrative>
  </description>
